    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="5.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 5.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5.3" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="52" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he self<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_5-3.lnote.oe.15"/> his wæpno<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_5-3.lnote.oe.16"/> his gefan utræcan wille, gehealden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_5-3.lnote.oe.17"/> hi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_5-3.lnote.oe.18"/> hine XXX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_5-3.lnote.oe.19"/> nihta ⁊ hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_5-3.lnote.oe.20"/> hine his mægum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_5-3.lnote.oe.21"/> gebodien.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5.3" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="52" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he sylf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_5-3.lnote.oe.7"/> his wæpna his gefán utræcan wille, gehealdon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_5-3.lnote.oe.3"/> hi hine XXX nihta ⁊ hi hine his magum gebodie.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_5-3.lnote.oe.8"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5.3" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="53" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf he sylf his wæpno his gefán utrǽcan [wylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_5-3.lnote.oe.2"/>], gehealdan hi hine ðrittig nihta, ⁊ hi hine his magum gebeoden.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5.3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="53" ed="#liebermann"/>Si inimicis suis arma sua reddiderit et se dederit, seruetur XXX noctibus et parentibus et amicis suis interim offeratur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="66" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif he self his wæpno<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#Af_5-3.attnote.fn.12"/> his gefan utræcan wille, gehealden hi hine XXX nihta ⁊ hie hine his mægum gebodien<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#Af_5-3.attnote.fn.13"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="5.3" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="298" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif he self his wæpno his gefan utræcan wille, gehealden hi hine XXX nihta ⁊ hie hine his mægum gebodien.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="53" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn er selbst seine Waffen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_5-3.lnote.de.1"/> seinen Verfolgern hinausreichen will, so sollen sie ihn 30 Nächte bewahren und ihn seinen Verwandten anzeigen.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_5-3.lnote.de.2"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If he himself wishes to hand out his weapons to his pursuers, let them keep him 30 nights and notify his kinsmen of him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="67" ed="#attenborough"/>If he himself is willing to hand over his weapons to his enemies, they shall hold him in their power for thirty days; and they shall send formal notice of his position to his kinsmen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="411" ed="#whitelock"/>If he himself will hand out his weapons to his foes, they are to keep him for 30<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Af_5-3.whinote.n.2"/> days, and send notice about him to his kinsmen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="299" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If he himself is willing to hand over his weapons to his foes, let them hold him for 30 nights and let them announce this to his kinsmen.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="237"><label>cf. (inward disposition of offender)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-13">Af El 13</ref> <quote>For Alfred, it is the inward disposition of the offender that is crucial ... cf. MP §16; Alfred §5.3 and §44.1 [L 42.1].</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-sanctuary" n="135"><label>contrast</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_5">Ine 5–5.1</ref> <quote>Comparison of this law (which Wormald suggested served as a model for Alfred’s) with the laws on church sanctuary in the domboc makes clear that Alfred’s innovations, insofar as Ine’s laws may be held representative, are substantial.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-sanctuary" n="135"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Af_42-1">Af 42.1</ref> <quote>Requirements of this sort are imposed not only on those seeking the protection of churches (where one would expect them given concerns about the defilement of a consecrated building with blood), but even on those attacked while within their own dwellings.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-sanctuary" n="147, n. 75"><label>analogue</label> Penitential of Theodore I.iv.4–5 <quote>the injunction to abandon one’s weapons, which is a stereotypical element of penances imposed for homicide</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-sanctuary" n="147"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Af_1-8">Af 1.8</ref> <quote>the other instance of self-abandonment in Alfred’s laws … (cap. 1.8) … suggests that this and hence the similar clauses were conceived of with penance in mind</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-3.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sylf <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sylf So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-3.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-nu <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-nu So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-3.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-3.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hie <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hie So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-3.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þrittig <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þrittig So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-3.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hi <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hi Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-3.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mag. gebeoden <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mag. gebeoden Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-3.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-3.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-3.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> -ien</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read -ien</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_5-3.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. zugefügt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">added in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_5-3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘und sich ergibt’ Q richtig; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Waffe 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘and surrenders’ Q, correctly; <hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> Waffe 4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_5-3.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘anbieten’ B Q, ohne Änderung des Sinnes. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. o.</hi> 5⁹</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘offer’ B Q, without change of sense. <hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> 5⁹</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_5-3.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ebenso Af 42, 1; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Asyl 8; Sippe 16h</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Likewise Af 42, 1; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Asyl 8; Sippe 16h</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_5-3.attnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">66</biblScope></bibl><label>wæpno</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">wæpna</hi>. H. <hi rend="italic">-nu</hi> So. &amp; Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_5-3.attnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">66</biblScope></bibl><label>gebodien</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">gebeoden</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">gebodie</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Af_5-3.whinote.n.2" n="2" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">409</biblScope></bibl><label>30</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">from Exodus xxii. 18, but only wizards are mentioned there.</seg></note>
      </div>
